<<PlayBackgroundMusic Exciting_1>>
<<SetBGSprite "HutInterior">>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Excited">>
Ramu: I know we're keeping quiet for the neighbors, but my chest is making noise—Maa, Baba, you should've seen your boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: I saw the clay on his elbows and the shine in his eyes—enough seeing for a mother, speak softly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: What happened is done—tell it in short words, he has long pages tomorrow.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Excited">>
Ramu: Short words then—he held his spine like a flagpole, answered the crowd's shouts with silence, and when the moment got heavy, he turned it like a knob, one click at a time.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Bhai.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Excited">>
Ramu: Hush, champion. I won't tell the whole story—just this: he remembered the team before himself and twice chose the right option over the loud one.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Right options taste better than sweet ones, but the laddu of marks is still not cooked. Day after tomorrow morning, yes?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Yes, Maa. First paper.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Then tonight we eat simple, talk simple, and sleep simple—the brain learns best when the room is boring.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: I've already made boring into a plan—table of contents twice, dictation for new words, ten sums till they stop wobbling, then lights off with no hero tales.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Good, Raju—wash your feet again, mud doesn't enter a mind that needs to stay clean.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: I know the deal—ninety, and we heard it with both ears.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: You heard it, but did you taste it? Numbers have a flavor of sweat and ink—he can soak in applause for ten minutes, then he soaks in ink.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Baba, I'll bring the ink home—promise.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Promises are lighter than notebooks, beta—sit and open the page with the long division that bites you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Before we start—one minute for what your hands did well today, say it once, then we lock the ground outside and invite the pages in.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I waited and didn't try to win everything in one breath.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Good—remember that same waiting here, sums are also bowls of hot milk you sip, not gulp.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Ramu, put the trophy under the books.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Under?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Yes—let it carry the weight of tomorrow's work, and if it bends, it wasn't worth much.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Raju, today the ground said your name and day after tomorrow the paper will ask it in a hundred little ways. Write it with the same hand—neat, patient, no swagger.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I don't know how to swagger, Baba.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Good, keep it that way. Pride sits on a shoulder and makes the neck sore—we need your neck free for thinking.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Maa, when I close my eyes I can still hear the drum from the ground thumping here.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Then give it a new beat—"Read, write, check, next"—and keep tapping that till sleep comes.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Also, we're setting alarms—first bell revision, second bell breakfast, third bell leave early. I'll walk him to the gate even if the sky becomes a river.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Take an extra pencil, extra eraser, and that small hand towel—sweaty hands make silly mistakes.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Baba, Maa… if I get the ninety, then—

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: No "then" tonight—the only prize we discuss is a clean page and a calm head, and the rest is a door we'll knock on when the ink dries.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: He's ready—I vouch for his hours, not just his highlights.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: I believe your watch, but belief and permission are cousins, not twins. I'll keep my word—he brings me ninety percent, I walk him to that banyan and tell my fear to take a holiday.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Worried">>
Kamla: And if he brings eighty-nine?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: We shake his hand for trying and keep him here longer. The world is not kind, so let the rules be clear at home.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Last instruction for tonight, captain—when you close this notebook, close the stadium inside your head too, lock it with the key under the pillow. Tomorrow evening you can visit it again.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Day after tomorrow, the paper will ask if you can keep a promise—answer "yes" with numbers. Bring me ninety percent and the road to that academy opens; if not, it doesn't—no anger, no tears, clear skies, clear rules.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Understood—I accept.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Now let's make the home quiet enough for the answers to hear us.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
<<EndEvent>>
<<StopBackgroundMusic>>
<<wait 3>>

===